# Gate 3 - Tests Neutered

`it.only` silently passes a whole suite by running one test. `it.skip` and a
commented-out expectation are the quieter versions.

Three checks, computed fresh by `check.cjs` every render:

1. Zero `.only(` anywhere in `tests/`.
2. `.skip(` count never above the committed floor (`skip-floor.json`), and
   every occurrence carries a reason comment on the same or preceding line.
3. Total test count never drops below `scripts/test-baseline.json`'s
   recorded floor, the same file `npm run test:baseline` already checks,
   wired into this gate rather than duplicated.

